# Files Vercel does not need in the uploaded source.
#
# This is a DEPLOY-SIZE guard, not a source-control one. .gitignore decides
# what is committed; .vercelignore decides what is uploaded to build the site.
# Both are needed because `next build` must still be able to see the files it
# compiles, while everything else is dead weight on the wire.
#
# The single most important entry is RESEARCH TRASH: ~163MB of archived site,
# a browser profile, a nested node_modules and a capture harness. It is
# excluded from tsconfig already, so the build never reads it.

node_modules
.next
out
.vercel

# Archived previous passes. Not referenced by any route.
RESEARCH TRASH
**/tmp-shot/
**/edge-profile/
**/shots/

# Local notes and configuration that are not part of the built site.
.gitignore
DESIGNS.md
ASIANCODER.MD
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
*.tsbuildinfo
*.log

# Editor and OS noise
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.pem